## Introduction

**MessageHook** is a .NET testing framework for Kafka-based integration testing. It provides:

- **End-to-End Message Flow Testing**: Produce messages to Kafka topics and consume the results
- **Two Consuming Modes**: Match responses by an auto-generated correlation ID, or by a known Kafka message key
- **Easy Setup**: A single `services.AddKafkaMessageHook(...)` call wires up everything

This guide walks through setting up integration tests for a Kafka-based service using MessageHook, and it tracks the actual test projects shipped in this repository — [`MessageHook.Tests`](MessageHook.Tests) (xUnit) and [`MessageHook.NUnit`](MessageHook.NUnit) (NUnit). Where this guide shows code, that code is the real code from those projects (or a trivial adaptation of it), so you can always cross-check against the source.

