## Step 5: Define Topic and Group Constants

Create one consts class per test project with the Kafka topic and group names it needs. This is the real, current `TestConsts.cs` from `MessageHook.Tests/Consts` (the `MessageHook.NUnit` copy is identical, just in the `MessageHook.NUnit.Consts` namespace):

```csharp
namespace MessageHook.Tests.Consts;

public class TestConsts
{
    // Producer
    public const string PRODUCER_ANIMAL = "A";

    // Consumer
    public const string CONSUMER_GROUP = "Automation-MessageHook-Tests";
    public const string CONSUMER_TOPIC = "B";
}
```

Replace `PRODUCER_ANIMAL` / `CONSUMER_TOPIC` with your own input/output topic names, and give `CONSUMER_GROUP` a name unique to your project so test runs don't collide with anyone else's consumer group.

