## Best Practices

### 1. Use Unique Consumer Groups

```csharp
// ✅ Good - unique per test project
public const string CONSUMER_GROUP = "Automation-MessageHook-Tests";

// ❌ Bad - generic name might conflict
public const string CONSUMER_GROUP = "test-group";
```

### 2. Always Clean Up in a `finally` Block

```csharp
try
{
    // test body
}
finally
{
    await DeleteConsumerGroupAsync();
}
```

### 3. Set Appropriate Timeouts

```csharp
TimeOut = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30)  // fast services
TimeOut = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(60)  // slower processing
TimeOut = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(2)   // batch operations
```

### 4. Async/Await Correctly

```csharp
// ✅ Good
var messages = await waitForMessagesTask.Task;

// ❌ Bad - can deadlock
var messages = waitForMessagesTask.Task.Result;
```

### 5. Don't Set ExpectedMessageKey When Producing

`ExpectedMessageKey` is for consume-by-key flows. When you call `ExecuteAsync(key, message)` to produce, MessageHook generates the correlation ID for you — leave `ExpectedMessageKey` unset.

